# WAVc: an FM bell. A sine modulator at 3.5 times the voice's note (not heard)
# phase-modulates a sine carrier; an env sweeps the index from 5 down to 0
# in the first 200 ms of each note, so the note starts bright and inharmonic
# and settles to a pure tone at its pitch; a second env shapes the level.
# melo plays A3, C4, E4, A4 (ratio=1 is 220 Hz times the note's pitch). Nothing
# is NaN or over 0 dBFS, the notes land on the grid, and once the index has
# swept down each note is within 5 cents of its pitch.
# scn: length 8b, seed 0, assets click
# expect: peak <= 0dbfs
# expect: peak >= -12dbfs
# expect: onsets on main every 1b within 64f in 0b..0.02b
# expect: onsets on main every 1b within 64f in 0.90b..1.02b
# expect: onsets on main every 1b within 64f in 1.90b..2.02b
# expect: onsets on main every 1b within 64f in 2.90b..3.02b
# expect: onsets on main every 1b within 64f in 3.90b..4.02b
# expect: onsets on main every 1b within 64f in 4.90b..5.02b
# expect: onsets on main every 1b within 64f in 5.90b..6.02b
# expect: pitch 0.7b..0.95b 220hz within 5c
# expect: pitch 1.7b..1.95b 261.63hz within 5c
# expect: pitch 2.7b..2.95b 329.63hz within 5c
# expect: pitch 3.7b..3.95b 440hz within 5c
# expect: pitch 4.7b..4.95b 220hz within 5c
# expect: equals golden
voice bell gain=0.5 {
  wave m ratio=3.5 out=no
  wave c ratio=1 fm=m index=0
  env bright to=c.index depth=5 attack=0 decay=200ms sustain=0
  env amp to=c.gain attack=2ms decay=700ms sustain=0
  seq notes 1 2 3 4 in 4 | melo bell 60 63 67 72
}
start bell
end after 7
